cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "CERNAL — Compiler-like Engine for RNA Logic"
message: "If you use CERNAL in your research, please cite it as below."
type: software
# TODO before the GitLab freeze: replace the collective author with the individual
# team members who should receive citation credit (given-names / family-names pairs),
# and add the repository-code URL once the iGEM GitLab repo exists.
authors:
  - name: "iGEM TAU 2026 Team, Tel Aviv University"
    city: "Tel Aviv"
    country: IL
    website: "https://2026.igem.wiki/tau-israel"
abstract: >-
  CERNAL is a design platform for RNA logic circuits. It takes transcriptomic
  differential-expression data and a biological objective, discovers candidate trigger
  RNAs, designs logic gates over them, and returns ranked circuit candidates with
  scores, metrics, sequences and reproducible artifacts.
keywords:
  - synthetic biology
  - RNA logic circuits
  - toehold switch
  - transcriptomics
  - iGEM
license: Apache-2.0
version: "0.1.0"
